# The Almquist shell px48 holds PAX's job control to (tools/fetch-busybox).
#
# The contract asked for "a static dash (the Debian/Ubuntu package's
# binary)"; no distribution packages one (Ubuntu 24.04's, Debian's and
# Alpine's dash are dynamic PIE, which PAX's loader refuses by name:
# notes/px48-job-control.md §2). Ubuntu 24.04's busybox-static is a
# distribution package's static binary (ET_EXEC, no PT_INTERP), and its
# `sh` is BusyBox's ash, the Almquist shell dash also descends from. It
# is run, never read: the .deb from Ubuntu's archive BY DIGEST, the one
# file taken out of it by its own digest, nothing built.
BUSYBOX_VERSION=1:1.36.1-6ubuntu3.1
BUSYBOX_URL=http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/b/busybox/busybox-static_1.36.1-6ubuntu3.1_amd64.deb
BUSYBOX_DEB_SHA256=944b2728f53ceb3916cec2c962873c9951e612408099601751db2a0a5d81e0ed
BUSYBOX_SHA256=dbac288c29ba568459550a2da9e7ae0ded6b1fc728ee9fad3044c44e62d6ac14
